WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — rce-jepa (45s) Narrator Jyothi

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.403
First, instead of guessing raw code word by word,

2
00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:07.100
small models predict compact summaries of program meaning.

3
00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:11.204
Second, any AI model may propose a candidate program,

4
00:00:11.204 --> 00:00:14.453
but a fast, strict checker decides what passes.

5
00:00:14.893 --> 00:00:19.939
Third, checking uses seventeen hundred times less energy than generating,

6
00:00:19.939 --> 00:00:22.565
and saved fixes slash big model calls.

7
00:00:23.005 --> 00:00:30.720
Generating one candidate with a local thirty-five-billion-parameter model burns eighty-four joules with zero safety guarantees.

8
00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:38.496
Checking a Reality Code Engine blueprint takes forty-nine millijoules—so any model can suggest, while only the inspector admits.

9
00:00:38.936 --> 00:00:41.981
With up to five rounds of exact checker feedback,

10
00:00:41.981 --> 00:00:48.631
frontier models close all forty open repair tasks, and saving those fixes cuts recurring calls sixteenfold.
